    "turn_text": "our democracy, attacks against our education system, attacks against our children, against women, telling us what we can or cannot do with our own bodies. And we have a huge affordability crisis that we're facing. So I've been traveling the state now for quite some time and families all over the state. Whether I'm talking to students at FAMU in the northern part of the state or seniors in Orlando, it's the same thing people can't afford to live here. And so we need someone in the Senate that's going to put the interest of our families above anything else, above politics. And we have right now in the Senate, the worst senator, someone that oversaw the largest Medicare fraud in the history of this country. He took $64 million of that money to buy his Senate seat, and he could care less about the struggles that we're facing here. He has no idea what it's like for people like my mom who have to live on that fake social security check or for those young adults that can't even move out of their homes because they can't afford to pay for their rent in their apartments. And so I'm running because those opportunities are disappearing. And because of those opportunities, I'm right now talking to you as the Senate candidate running against Scott for the US Senate. I came here when I was 14. My mom brought me here at a very young age. She worked 12-hour shifts, two jobs to make ends meet. I started working at the age of 15 at a minimum wage job. And this is an incredible country, a country that has always given those opportunities, regardless of race, regardless of background, that if you work hard enough and you have people behind you, anything is possible. And that's why I'm running. I want to make sure that everyone everyone in the state realizes their potential that they know what is possible if we come together and reminding them that when we come out, when we vote, we can win these races. And I've been feeling that energy all across Florida.",
