  {
    "episode_id": 95657,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95657.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 133,
    "turn_text": "Maddie, everywhere I've gone. I mean, I've been talking to people from across party lines, Republicans, independents, Democrats. No one trusts Rick Scott. They know that he's a fraud. They know that he, when he was CEO of HCA, that healthcare company, Columbia HCA, he oversaw the largest Medicare fraud in the history of this country. They had to pay out $1.7 billion, the largest Medicare fraud that we have ever seen here in the United States. That's who he is. People in Florida have realized that not only is he a fraud, but he also has been using that Senate seat for self enrichment. They know that he wrote a plan that would eliminate Medicare and Social Security that would raise taxes in middle class families that would take away funding for the Department of Education. I mean, This is a man that's extremely dangerous. I want the entire country to pay attention to who he is. He can't go under the radar. And this is the opportunity for us to once and for all vote him out. People are excited about my candidacy. My story is the story of so many people across the state that with hard work and through those opportunities they've been able. to come here to the state and thrive and all of a sudden they're seeing that these failed policies are choking them from those opportunities, right? So they're excited to see that there's someone that has a really, really strong chance. I'm going to be the first Latina Democrat to ever be on the top of the ticket and I'm going to be the only Latina running at the top of the tickets nationwide. That's a huge, huge win for women, Latina women across our country. But I can't believe that it's 2024 and it's taken this long for us to be able to nominate somebody like myself with the background that I have. I was the first person that was elected to serve in the US House of Representatives as a South American immigrant. I don't want to be the first. I don't want to be the last. I feel the same way about the Senate. I think that we need to continue to work to pave the way for young women that want to that have their eye on getting into politics that want to serve, that want to be in public service. And we have a lot of responsibilities to do that. So I think that people are excited. I am a woman who will absolutely put women's rights above anything else. I have two daughters. I have a son. This is also a very important issue. I don't want to have my daughters living in a state where now they are living with less rights than what I've lived under here in this country. And so much is at stake. And in Florida, the uniqueness of the political landscape here is that people have been feeling those attacks for the past few years. And we are done with extremism, and they don't represent our values. Don't for a second think just because Donald Trump moved his residency here. All of a sudden, it's a state that is fully behind Donald Trump. I have talked to Republicans. many times and many Republicans across the state that will not support what is going on right now in the",
