    "turn_idx": 138,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, because this is a top of mind issue and it really is affecting everyone. And it's all I hear when I talk to Floridians, the first policy paper that we've released and we did it a couple of months ago already is an affordability plan. And we can reduce the rates of property insurance here in the state of Florida at the federal level. People realize that this is a statewide issue, that it's come from extreme Republicans. It's that it actually started under Rick Scott. He took tens of thousands of dollars in campaign contributions from insurance companies, then took $50 million from the public option and gave it to his campaign donors and his friends. And so this crisis started under his leadership when he was here as governor. There's a bill right now in the house. Sammy that we can introduce in the Senate that would lower property insurance rates by 25%. That's significant for people here living in the state of Florida. I would love to be able to lead that bill and make sure that we pass it. I've already talked to some senators about that. So that is possible and it's a possibility, but we need to invest in resiliency, right? We have communities here all over the state. They're coastal communities with many, many small businesses, which are really an economic engine. for our economy in the state. And we are entering a summer where we're already getting ready for some very severe weather and severe storms. Yet we have not invested in resiliency. And Rick Scott voted against billions of dollars that would bring that funding down to the state. And that also affects property insurance rates. So that's something else that's included in my plan. We also need to make sure that we bring good paying jobs to our state. Unfortunately, a lot of people your age are leaving Florida because they can't find a good paying job. There are other opportunities for them to leave. Well, we can bring jobs by investing in solar energy. We need to make sure that we attract more tech companies to come and, and bring their innovation here to the state of Florida. There are a lot of things that we can do. Unfortunately, our leaders could care less, right? I mean, the, the, the politicos that have been in office like Rick Scott for 14 years, they could",
