    "turn_text": "You know, I've been going to the Florida Keys for years and years and years. And when my kids were babies, we would go to the florida keys. We continue to do that. My sister now has a house. We're really lucky that she finally got a house in the keys. And so it's my favorite spot. The minute I start driving down US one and I see water on on both sides on our drive. I mean, there's so many interesting places to visit in the keys. You can have really incredible food all over. There's some great, great restaurants are great. places for people to say, you can go kayaking, you can go boating, you can go fishing. There are beautiful parks with great beaches. It's an incredible place. And only in the United States, the only living coral reefs are along the Florida Keys. And I'm a huge coral reef lover. I did a lot of work with Coral Restoration Foundation. And actually, you should check out my ad that I did in 2018. It was a scuba diving ad because our reefs are really facing some serious threats with more warming of the oceans. And I actually, with a Republican, passed a bill to protect our coral reefs when I was in Congress. So it has a very special place in my heart. I represented the keys when I was in Congress, and we go there as often as we can with the kids.",
