    "turn_text": "carbon emissions. They understand that we need to transition to green energy. I mean, look at the amount of electric vehicles that we're now manufacturing. And we need to make sure that these electric vehicles have the infrastructure ready for them. which is why those investments from that infrastructure bill are so crucial that people are not seeing yet. But we're going to have those charging stations increase all across the country. Those are the type of things that we need to move to. But companies and business owners understand this. They really do see it. The agricultural industry all over the country, I think, has realized that they need to control any sort of pollution and runoff and what they're using in their farms because it's polluting the water. And then if the water is polluted, It goes down to the ocean. If the ocean sees high levels of pollution, it will affect tourism. It will affect the fisheries. Everything is connected. And here in the state of Florida, it's not a tough conversation to have. Most people understand that it's an issue that we need to continue to work on. There's this organization called Vote Water. So it's not Republican, it's not Democrats, it's vote water and they endorsed me back in 2018 and 2020. And they're already talking to their members that Rick Scott has been the worst person as it relates to our climate and our environment. Why? Because he's making money off of big oil. I mean, that's the reality. They are completely linked to the special interests that prevent the country for moving forward. And we should be in the forefront of addressing these challenges, especially in the Sunshine State. We should have more solar panels than other places in the country, yet we do not because we are giving favors to those special interests. And so we were falling behind in the United States. There are other countries that are doing much more as it pertains to climate and green energy and transitioning to green energy. 